ETHICAL PRINCIPLES
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Every person has the right to understand their own body and their own health
data — regardless of disability, chronic illness, gender identity, age,
educational background, income, or digital literacy. This right belongs to
everyone, not only to those with medical or technical training.

This project exists to make that right real: through self-determination,
informed agency, and full ownership of one's own data — without surveillance,
lock-in, or extractive design.

See docs/ETHICS.md (English) and docs/ETHICS_DE.md (Deutsch) for the full
ethical principles, including prohibited uses, security requirements, and
guidelines for research with human subjects.


